    desc: "Museumcore is a mood-board aesthetic that aestheticises the museum itself: marble busts, gilded frames, plinths, velvet ropes, conservators' gloves, wall labels and echo-filled galleries. It grew on Tumblr and Instagram in the late 2010s beside dark academia, sharing its library-and-blazer mood but swapping books for vitrines — the fantasy is curated quiet, cultural capital and clean light. Imagery borrows from institution photography: the Louvre's crowds, the Met's period rooms, natural-history dioramas, archival drawers, in marble white, graphite, oxblood velvet and brass. Community context skews to aspirational students and art workers posting study-in-the-gallery scenes; museums have adopted the tag. Trajectory: a background aesthetic feeding dark academia playlists, gallery Instagram culture and stationery lines — a -core built on public institutions rather than private nostalgia.",
