    desc: "Royalcore is a fashion-and-fantasy aesthetic centred on European royal court imagery: tiaras, ballgowns, corsetry, gloves, crests, gilded palaces and elaborate etiquette. It developed from Tumblr royalty mood boards in the late 2010s and surged after Netflix's Bridgerton (2020), which drove a Regency wave on TikTok under names like regencycore; CARI documents it in its corpus. Vocabulary borrows from portraits of European courts, coronation regalia, period-drama set design and royal-wedding broadcast culture. Community context is performative and aspirational: your-highness address memes, ballroom-style dances, tea ceremonies and hobbyist historical dance and costume communities ground it offline. Trajectory: royalcore overlaps princesscore (softer, childlike) and dark academia (scholastic, not courtly); it has fed corset and occasion-wear trends and persists as a durable roleplay tag.",
