    desc: "Princesscore is the softer, more childlike branch of the royal fantasy family: tulle skirts, big bows, heart lockets, glass slippers, storybook castles and a pervasive pink glow. Where Royalcore plays at adult courtly power, Princesscore reconstructs the fairy-tale image set of the Disney VHS era and picture-book illustration — pink-and-lilac palettes, glitter and round friendly shapes. It consolidated on Tumblr and Pinterest in the late 2010s and continues on TikTok, with CARI documenting it in its corpus. Community context is comfort-seeking and often self-aware: users pair princess imagery with captions about gentleness and protecting one's inner child, and it overlaps costume-play communities. Trajectory: princesscore fed tulle occasion-fashion trends and coquette-adjacent styling, a stable tag family alongside Lovecore and Angelcore, marked by castle-and-storybook settings.",
