    sum: "Wires, terminals and HUD overlays: a bedroom-scale hacker fantasy softer than canon cyberpunk.",
    desc: "Cybercore is a mood-board aesthetic that condenses cyberpunk iconography into bedroom-scale internet life: tangled cables, LED strips, terminal windows, glitched readouts, circuit traces, mask-and-goggles styling, floating HUD overlays. It consolidated on Tumblr and Discord in the late 2010s as a tag distinct from canon Cyberpunk — less noir dystopia, more self-insert technophile comfort, often paired with webcore and glitch edits. Vocabulary mixes 1990s hacker-film UI, Y2K device design, vaporwave-adjacent grids and real maker culture (Raspberry Pis, solder, cable management), on black hardware against neon green, electric blue and magenta. Community context skews toward coding and modding hobbyists and security fandoms styling themselves as machine-assisted. Trajectory: an active tag family feeding esports and RGB-gamer styling, distinct in its persona-first framing.",
